#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054694 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054602 :question/id #uuid "6b16ff95-8b78-587d-a7c8-8d0909b69f19" :question/math-academy-id "e-983" :question/problem "Use the table below to plot the graph of $y=3x-2$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$, we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=3x-2$.\nTherefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=3(0)-2=-2$,\n- if $x=1$ then $y=3(1)-2=1$,\n- if $x=2$ then $y=3(2)-2=4$, and\n- if $x=3$ then $y=3(3)-2=7$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | $7$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/09/09e670353b2114b229769e2bd6b3eb4a9895389b818fc3f4ace6997a3e7efa3f.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=3x-2$.\n\n![](images/d2/d2d8891102ce99020f544bd8d82a5ff0454080474ce4267ef5285db92f5b2ca0.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2491cf6c-260b-5992-a910-9fe6a80e30bc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048714 :topic/math-academy-id 94 :topic/title "Two-Variable Linear Equations and Their Solutions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050517 :topic/math-academy-id 92 :topic/title "The Cartesian Coordinate System"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95871ea8-427c-5d8b-b7b9-90621fa03a1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a26ee2942f083a2edb99e9839d71577e1772bf6410e1ae4beafcde7f59c7109.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053458} {:answer/id #uuid "c7240b34-1c9b-5ca5-9452-e210e669f37a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/893dba533e0afffe05f9603293355ccf38b2723fcd91608ea03fe321e26a0d5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053459} {:answer/id #uuid "17588e8d-da64-5d6b-ab34-45af1c4a7804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/eaf735f72849b82e92f7baf0d991f3e024e013b66d9813d4e0d5f3a87632c901.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053460} {:answer/id #uuid "27023196-b279-5485-8ce7-7bf4dc0c7ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/afb9d602e1bff2fb643f44ed5dfa09d41833740e814739c60d5dd890a2f02270.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053461} {:answer/id #uuid "2a8ce376-c015-5edf-afdd-204f6ccb159f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/02f0d3d8bb1bd1e87d05e63579e2a92281de1d000fe2baa7c9942dd80b542efb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053462}] :answer-field/id #uuid "1bbe1741-021b-5eb6-8d9e-91ce5412b307" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053457}] :question/id #uuid "4524558d-8a83-5843-a336-69f66463c3a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-54397" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y = x - 2$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8012f237-f895-59fa-8270-6503cec53a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/33840084a698d261095927ca6ca12e85673665e3dc00264e1d21722a60c16fa4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053812} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce4d676-af93-589c-ba26-6402379e878e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/893dba533e0afffe05f9603293355ccf38b2723fcd91608ea03fe321e26a0d5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053813} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b7f4ba-210d-5ab9-a5f8-a2904e7fedf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/41/416bc4e441bac223991d615915c282fed3ecae8ececd4ce04433a1eacfad47f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053814} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e4e655-149e-5749-b055-169473ebdae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7e/7e1e94d8d56f09e4c5d2b47cbd04ec99d51f97465d8144683f16a5689fd6324c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053815} {:answer/id #uuid "40c8bec8-cf09-50fd-97ef-11e1dc5e4980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/eaf735f72849b82e92f7baf0d991f3e024e013b66d9813d4e0d5f3a87632c901.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053816}] :answer-field/id #uuid "423e8e65-dd75-5e41-82c6-09a914060bee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053811}] :question/id #uuid "4cd916a5-f5b2-585b-bea7-8dda3f5e10d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-59676" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y =-x + 1$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |"}] :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Line Using a Table"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054695 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054603 :question/id #uuid "4aad1578-4134-5f25-88cb-8ab4631257ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-984" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3$." :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\nIt is often easiest to pick one of the points to have an $x$-coordinate of $x=0$. So, for the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0$. Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= -\\frac{1}{2}x + 3 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}(0) + 3 \\\\\n&= 0 + 3 \\\\\n&= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,3)$.\n\nFor the second point, let's choose $x=4$. Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= -\\frac{1}{2}x + 3 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}(4) + 3 \\\\\n&=-2 + 3 \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(4,1)$.\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of\n\n$$\ny=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3\n$$\n\n![](images/36/36689081acaacb24a09826c3927388697e77d92caeca900d053d33d0f99d2b8c.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebeb4e5a-adbe-5a94-b05d-61933a687892" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0a3946e-4d98-5306-b4b2-f900a60e9abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ff/ff2f94655de95a7a5099423b3d0dbbb9bb6e64f39aca105eb8cab1366f547064.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053452} {:answer/id #uuid "f18a5b0b-4150-51bf-ae4a-e1621ffc7785" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8b/8bc5f7358456a111f29f900e8148e60a0fede85ca9b951e3d752ca1e1a800e6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053453} {:answer/id #uuid "15e16ea3-e05e-53e9-8ea7-ae8c5c48c14e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7e/7ed9a41dc38df65a985785c318e5d0407a43615cef7dfa0c60ad454099a089a9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053454} {:answer/id #uuid "2fb80dc2-f93b-5a21-82fe-a63bca5f9b7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0c/0cfc4bba4867b40c4c38b0886c37bb5c4cd64d293530ece7c67cdb6349134013.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053455} {:answer/id #uuid "3f60c829-2580-5c06-aab1-c1c58924a888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/06/0678cd88949fac3a9ce58d255eee9d8a07ba8c3b91a86f90fa24d70d1510568f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053456}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c2b4ae38-d4b8-5d3e-8141-6ba4d4385b82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053451}] :question/id #uuid "28feb85a-a0a4-55cd-b26b-1f144b97ee7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-54286" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y = 2x - 4$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055430 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b72f52d3-7c21-5555-bf79-a5e32ea63dc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9e/9e2977ee1faa5dde2d1bf3a427037aac75b2692486bdcb724356452765c8b661.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053818} {:answer/id #uuid "c7a6f114-0b92-53a7-be81-3901b4da5d29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0c/0cfc4bba4867b40c4c38b0886c37bb5c4cd64d293530ece7c67cdb6349134013.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053819} {:answer/id #uuid "eddea0ed-d911-5e32-b099-869db5076ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/45177c5e17c0040286e8404613e88f5f472417ae3a640ad7fb5fa6468646fedd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053820} {:answer/id #uuid "09a91346-d838-5250-81eb-a1248c4d8558" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9c/9c7577f7033f36315d50748424d7a8db635e9aecd4c88c9ed4626f3294bc6c2b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053821} {:answer/id #uuid "11cb7f7a-bdd2-52bd-aa97-ada840a3b84a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ff/ff2f94655de95a7a5099423b3d0dbbb9bb6e64f39aca105eb8cab1366f547064.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053822}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e6d1196c-1fdd-5a78-9a03-811c69c20b33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053817}] :question/id #uuid "f8b0e058-eb84-5845-9c9e-ed354a3b82f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-59678" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y = \\frac{1}{2}x - 2$?"}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching a Line Using Two Points"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054802 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054499 :question/id #uuid "2efe9f75-18c0-5a86-b56b-3f338b7e5c2d" :question/math-academy-id "e-1702" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the graph of the straight line below?\n\n1. $y=2x-1$\n2. $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1$\n3. $2x-y=1$\n\n![](images/93/93dc9d447c15e4597549996b1f0b533cf86783b5cc5df032a4c46d4ca8934abc.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, we can choose $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-1)$ and $(2,3)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/a9/a9f18453dedb1763908825301f80ef86307d3a3aceaf678bbe8579a42a0996f5.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=2x-1$.\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n$(-1)|= 2(0) - 1; - 1|=-1✓; (3)|= 2(2) - 1; 3|= 3✓$\nTherefore, $y=2x-1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n- Equation II: $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1$.\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n$(-1)|= \\frac{1}{2}(0) - 1; - 1|=-1✓; (3)|= \\frac{1}{2}(2) - 1; 3|= 0\\cdot$\nTherefore, $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $2x-y=1$.\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3)$, we obtain\n$2(0) - (-1)|= 1; 1|= 1✓; 2(2) - (3)|= 1; 1|= 1✓$\nTherefore, $2x-y=1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that represented the line in the graph were $y=2x-1$ and $2x-y=1$, corresponding to answer choices I and III. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3986a3cd-c543-54e9-8d55-f744d9436313" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86184d72-71eb-5266-97aa-98ca9333aac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053446} {:answer/id #uuid "f56f9fc1-a41f-52d1-a174-4f44b3a36e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053447} {:answer/id #uuid "38764fde-baad-5551-b71a-bb9e399ca769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053448} {:answer/id #uuid "5732fc71-f59d-5bbd-a6fc-3a658071237e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053449} {:answer/id #uuid "70ba90c3-8f12-5e6e-8510-a650716f0851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053450}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7beff78d-9b7e-5a87-a424-6ec7aa9ddf98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053445}] :question/id #uuid "56e71e28-d3a5-545f-bf8d-30361fbf20ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-54285" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4ce176ba6bb73da8d6af410bedad4733cf3e705c70e28f133d771b89f78130c5.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\n1. $y = x + \\frac{1}{2}$\n2. $y = \\frac{1}{2}x + 2$\n3. $y = \\frac{1}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c180d864-bc07-583b-a883-481866f09213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053824} {:answer/id #uuid "ff1c6236-4f98-5028-9df1-1a3d4feea252" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053825} {:answer/id #uuid "178a3569-9994-51b1-aeed-54d1afd7d5d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053826} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe2b615-e7df-5abb-a7ae-9fb5ebf64f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053827} {:answer/id #uuid "46f3ee86-cbf9-507f-944a-092d5e0e2256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053828}] :answer-field/id #uuid "31eb51f0-5d36-5ca2-a829-8a5c0c692be7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053823}] :question/id #uuid "2fe51fc5-fce7-5fb6-911c-f561e72ff3fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-59732" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d78eaaedd26a27d9163fdcddfce5c5ed429e441a75d361f0840935fce9235c6.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\n1. $x + 2y = 4$\n2. $y = 2 - x$\n3. $y = 4 - x$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Line Given a Graph"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054803 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054574 :question/id #uuid "ae9cba85-b0ed-59c9-bf9f-682b921c5ee4" :question/math-academy-id "e-6258" :question/problem "Given that $(x-1)$ and $(x-3)$ are factors of the polynomial $f(x)= x^4 - x^3 - 7 x^2 + x + 6,$ factor $f(x)$ completely." :question/worked-solution "To factor $f(x)$ completely, we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x-1)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x-1)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-1)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | $x^4$ | $x^3$ | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}1$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-7$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-7$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $0$ | $-7$ | $-6$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^4 - x^3 - 7 x^2 + x + 6}{x-1} = x^3-7x-6,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx^4 - x^3 - 7 x^2 + x + 6 = (x-1) (x^3-7x-6).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x-3)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $(x^3-7x-6).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x-3)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | $x^3$ | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-7$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $3$ | $9$ | $6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^3-7x-6}{x-3} = x^2+3x +2,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx^4 - x^3 - 7 x^2 + x + 6 =  (x-1) (x-3) (x^2+3x +2).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\nx^4 - x^3 - 7 x^2 + x + 6 =  (x-1) (x-3) (x+2)(x+1).\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e897cc-b3fe-5d2f-8b47-3afdfe276bcf" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048497 :topic/math-academy-id 2119 :topic/title "Factoring Cubic Polynomials Using the Factor Theorem"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "982b97fb-6a3a-5c8c-8476-20fcf0f687c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052406}] :question/id #uuid "6b1e280b-fba4-5891-88fc-5a7c6d06c02c" :question/math-academy-id "q-270966" :question/problem "The polynomial\n$-5x^{4} + 8x^{3} + 29x^{2} - 20x - 12$\ncan be expressed as\n$- (x - 1)(x - 3) \\cdot P(x)$.\nFind the polynomial $P(x)$.$P(x) =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b73fb732-c827-51b5-97ad-ba12f00a8502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 2)(x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054154} {:answer/id #uuid "121b62e6-58c9-5cd8-a11f-9637a651f542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1 - x)(x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054155} {:answer/id #uuid "2b0578df-e0b2-549e-840c-a126b907d2c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - 1)(x + 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054156} {:answer/id #uuid "5fdb57bd-1a8e-588c-9eb3-8aed53bf62e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1)(4 - x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054157} {:answer/id #uuid "7b66aa41-7b18-5a83-bc92-114e28a181aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x + 1)(x - 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054158}] :answer-field/id #uuid "41b9e11e-b5e8-5bb4-9b08-05f9cb0de09d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186054153}] :question/id #uuid "6573d8e0-c3bf-5172-9e20-d7cf0a1fe1d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-75709" :question/problem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that\n\n$x^{4} - 3x^{3} - 8x^{2} + 12x + 16 = (x + 1)(x - 4)P(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186